-- title:
--   A simplex cover has at least as many slots as diagonal AP parameters
-- statement:
--   For a positive modulus $N$, a natural $r$, and a finite cyclic set $A$, suppose a family of deleted coloured faces meets every labelled simplex of the $(r+2)$-colour AP hypergraph of $A$. Then
--
--   $$
--   |A|N^r\le\sum_j|D_j|.
--   $$
--
--   The left side counts the diagonal AP parameters: a member of $A$ together with the $r$ free simplex coordinates. No primality or coefficient-coprimality assumption on $N$ is required.
